  "caption": "Quinn joined the cabin crew: so many overhead bags, then a hotel bed at 3pm with a very confused body clock.\n\nFlying can be hard on the body. Long periods seated, lifting bags overhead, pushing carts and broken sleep across time zones can all add up, and pilots deal with vibration and fixed positions on top.\n\nWhat often helps: set up your seat and change position regularly, keep bags close and ask for help with heavy ones, do a short bodyweight or band routine on layovers, and stay hydrated with good shoes. Compression socks may help puffy legs.\n\nOne swollen, painful leg, chest pain or shortness of breath needs urgent care. Persistent headaches are worth a GP visit.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
